---
description: Studium UI tokens and adaptive layout (SwiftUI)
globs: Studium/**/*.swift
alwaysApply: false
---

- **Design tokens:** Typography, spacing, and shell dimensions live in `Studium/Views/Components/MacStudiumDesign.swift` and are shared across iOS, iPadOS, and macOS. Prefer adjusting that file instead of scattering magic numbers.
- **Wide vs compact:** When root width `>= LayoutMetrics.macWideBreakpoint` (900pt), Practice uses **split** `widePracticeSplitLayout` (filter sidebar + browse column). Below that, Practice uses the **compact** shell: same filter blocks and `sidebarPracticeRow` stacked vertically, then Continue (if any), then `ExpandedConceptCard` in a single column.
- **Concept cards:** Always **`ExpandedConceptCard`** with `MacStudiumDesign.concept*` (no separate collapsible list style).
- **Continue / saved quiz strip:** Cards are **fixed width** `MacStudiumDesign.continueCardWidth`, **no `Spacer` filler** inside the card; intrinsic height from content.
- **Quiz:** Split-pane uses `MacStudiumDesign.quiz*` insets and spacing. On **iOS / iPad**, `useSplitPaneQuizLayout` is true when `quizViewportWidth >= LayoutMetrics.macWideBreakpoint` (same threshold as Practice). macOS is always split. Section labels use subheadline in split pane; primary actions use `.controlSize(.large)` when split-pane.
